# `push_batch_within`'s budget bound, spending one attempt more than it should.
#
# The whole `ring_poll` retry loop looks untestable from a single thread.
# Nothing changes between attempts, so a repeated attempt can only find the same
# answer. That is true of `push_within` and `recv_within`, whose survivors are
# in ../accepted/ for exactly that reason. It is false here, and the difference
# is what this declaration exists to hold.
#
# `ring_core::Producer::try_push_batch` pulls a record from the iterator before
# it can know whether there is room, so a refusal consumes and drops the record
# it could not place. That crate's own doctest pins this as intended. So every
# extra attempt against a full ring destroys one more record, and the attempt
# count is observable after all: not in the published total, not in the
# consumer's length, but in what is left of the caller's iterator.
#
# `try_push` hands the record back on failure. `try_push_batch` eats it. That is
# the entire difference between this file and the two accepted survivors.

id: S7
crate: ring_poll
file: src/lib.rs
round: 2026-08-30
round-failures: 1
detector: push_batch_within_eats_one_record_per_attempt

--- from
  while attempt < budget.attempts() {
    let moved = producer.try_push_batch(records);
--- to
  while attempt <= budget.attempts() {   // PROBE ONLY — G12, was `<`
    let moved = producer.try_push_batch(records);
--- end
